<===> README.md
A module loaded with `meta.load-css()` and then imported again evaluates its
`@use ... with` rules a second time. Their parent configuration (the one of
`meta.load-css()`) must still be valid then (it was a stack object).
<===>
================================================================================
<===> use_with/input.scss
@use "sass:meta";
@include meta.load-css("n");
@import "n";
<===> use_with/_n.scss
@use "x" with ($a: 1);
<===> use_with/_x.scss
$a: 0 !default;
b {c: $a}
<===> use_with/error
Error: This module was already loaded, so it can't be configured using "with".
  ,
1 | @use "x" with ($a: 1);
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ new load
  | ===================== original load
  '
  _n.scss 1:1     @import
  input.scss 3:9  root stylesheet
<===> use_with/error-libsass
Error: This module was already loaded, so it can't be configured using "with".
  ,
1 | @use "x" with ($a: 1);
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  _n.scss 1:1     @import
  ,
3 | @import "n";
  |         ^^^
  '
  input.scss 3:9  root stylesheet
